{
  "id": "proj-cedar-raised-garden-bed",
  "slug": "cedar-raised-garden-bed",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Cedar Raised Garden Bed",
  "summary": "A 4 x 8 ft bed, about 17 in deep, from cedar fence pickets screwed to cedar corner posts. Lined with hardware cloth to keep gophers out.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 4,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Clear and level a 4 x 8 ft patch of ground in a spot that gets at least six hours of sun.",
    "Cut the dog-ear tops off the pickets, then cut them into 48 in short-side boards and 72 in plus 24 in long-side boards (three courses per side).",
    "Cut the 2x2 cedar into six 17 in posts: one in each corner and one where the long-side boards butt together.",
    "Lay two posts on the ground and screw three short-side boards across them with two 1 1/4 in screws per board end; repeat for the other end.",
    "Stand the two ends up and screw the long-side boards on, butting the 72 in and 24 in pieces over a middle post, so every joint lands on wood.",
    "Flip the frame, cover the bottom with two overlapping strips of hardware cloth, staple it every 3 in, and trim the edges with tin snips while wearing gloves.",
    "Set the bed in place, check it is level, and fill it with a mix of topsoil and compost."
  ],
